  "TM0058": {
    "source": "Plano de ubicacion, Portal 80, version diciembre de 2025.",
    "why": "NOT a ring. Portal 80 draws two long lozenges lying diagonally, each bending once in the middle, with no turnaround loop anywhere — so it uses `andenes` (a platform as a thick round-capped polyline) where Portal Norte uses `anillo`. The axes and the 92px thickness were measured by taking the platform grey as a mask and walking each connected piece column by column (_eje.mjs); the four kerbs were then sampled directly across the width, which is what fixes the bend: Plataforma 1 turns at about x 555 and Plataforma 2 at about x 600. Chips here are drawn BIGGER than at Norte — 40px wide for a three-character code against 27 — so the chip metrics are part of the geometry rather than a constant.",
